          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Under
            %em Maxwell-Chern-Simons theories
            one understands
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theories"} Lagrangian field theories
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            content is a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            (locally on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-form"} differential 1-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = \mathrm{d}A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
            of that of (vacuum)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxwell+theory"} Maxwell theory
            with that of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+Chern-Simons+theory"} abelian Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            This means, over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 3
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi L
                    %mi MCS
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                      %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∝
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo −
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L_{MCS}^{3D}(A)
                  \\;\propto\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}
                  F \wedge \star F
                  \\;-\;
                  \\tfrac{c}{2} A \wedge F
                  \\,.
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            are (where we include the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
            in the first line in order to highlight the comparison to
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxwell%27s+equations"} Maxwell's equations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                          %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                          %mo ⋆
                          %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi c
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi F
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\mathrm{d} F &amp; = 0
                  \\\
                  \\mathrm{d} \star F &amp; = c \,F
                  \\,.
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            Similarly, there are higher dimensional versions. For instance over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D =5
            and using the Lagrangian density of abelian
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Chern-Simons+theory"} D=5 Chern-Simons theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi L
                    %mi MCS
                    %mrow
                      %mn 5
                      %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∝
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo −
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi c
                      %mn 3
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L_{MCS}^{5D}(A)
                  \\;\propto\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}
                  F \wedge \star F
                  \\;-\;
                  \\tfrac{c}{3} A \wedge F \wedge F
          %p
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
          #eq:EoMof5dMCS.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                          %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                          %mo ⋆
                          %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi c
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi F
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi F
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\mathrm{d} F &amp; = 0
                  \\\
                  \\mathrm{d} \star F &amp; = c \,F \wedge F
                  \\,.
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            This appears notably in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+field"} bosonic
            sector of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+supergravity"} D=5 supergravity
            (which is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Maxwell+theory"} Einstein-Maxwell
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Chern-Simons+theory"} D=5 Chern-Simons theory
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#DimReductionOf5dMaxwellCSTo3D Dimensional reduction of 5D Maxwell-Chern-Simons to 3D
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensional+reduction"} dimensional reduction
            of the 5D Maxwell-Chern-Simons equations of motion
